From 30aa2e48962c6e4cd5258840f55f2f413b0bdbb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milo Kim <woogyom.kim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Dec 2016 15:28:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: am335x: Fix the interrupt name of TPS65217

Use 'interrupt-names' for getting the charger interrupt number.

Fixes: 1934e89a769b ("ARM: dts: am335x: Add the charger interrupt")
Signed-off-by: Milo Kim <woogyom.kim@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Tony Lindgren <tony@atomide.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/am335x-bone-common.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
index dc561d505bbe..14b62690c464 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
@@ -320,7 +320,7 @@ &tps {

 	charger {
 		interrupts = <TPS65217_IRQ_AC>, <TPS65217_IRQ_USB>;
-		interrupts-names = "AC", "USB";
+		interrupt-names = "AC", "USB";
 		status = "okay";
 	};

-- 
2.25.1

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the incorrect use of the property name `interrupts-names` instead of the correct `interrupt-names` in the device tree source file. This misnaming prevented the system from properly retrieving the charger interrupt number, leading to potential issues in handling charger interrupts.

        Commit message:
        ARM: dts: am335x: Fix the interrupt name of TPS65217

Use 'interrupt-names' for getting the charger interrupt number.

Fixes: 1934e89a769b ("ARM: dts: am335x: Add the charger interrupt")
Signed-off-by: Milo Kim <woogyom.kim@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Tony Lindgren <tony@atomide.com>  

        Patch:
         	charger {
 		interrupts = <TPS65217_IRQ_AC>, <TPS65217_IRQ_USB>;
-		interrupts-names = "AC", "USB";
+		interrupt-names = "AC", "USB";
 		status = "okay";
 	};


        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Code statements:
        <text1>
        <text2>
        ...
        <textN>
